# bat's settings. bat is cat with syntax highlighting; it reads this file from
# ~/.config/bat (BAT_CONFIG_DIR in ~/.config/zsh/.zshenv points there).
# One bat command-line option per line; defaults are unchanged.

# Catppuccin Mocha is one of bat's built-in themes (bat --list-themes lists them).
--theme="Catppuccin Mocha"

# Use the theme's italics (comments, functions, parameters); Ghostty renders them.
--italic-text=always

# Show line numbers, Git modifications and file header (but no grid).
--style="numbers,changes,header"
